pseudo-Boolean proof version 3.0
% The same defect one width up, in `GeneralPBConstraint::<i128>`: the degree `i128::MIN` does
% not fit `i64` but does fit `i128`, so the row is stored in the wider type and the wrap simply
% moves to that type's boundary. Widening is not a fix; checked arithmetic is.
f 2;
rup 1 x2 >= -170141183460469231731687303715884105728 ;
red 1 ~x1 >= 1 : x1 -> 1 ;
pol 1 4 +;
output NONE;
conclusion UNSAT : 5;
end pseudo-Boolean proof;
